== Mock Examination 2 — Questions

#mcq(1, [The speed of a nerve impulse is increased by], [a thinner axon], [a larger diameter and a myelin sheath], [more dendrites], [a larger nucleus])

#mcq(2, [The aqueous humour is found], [behind the retina], [in the middle ear], [in the cochlea], [between the cornea and the lens])

#mcq(3, [The root of a plant grows downwards because of], [positive geotropism], [negative geotropism], [phototropism], [thigmotropism])

#mcq(4, [The coconut is dispersed by], [wind], [animals], [water], [explosion])

#mcq(5, [The zygote divides to form a ball of cells that implants in the], [oviduct], [cervix], [endometrium of the uterus], [ovary])

#mcq(6, [The fast growth of infancy is an adaptation that], [allows the baby to walk soon], [reduces the need for food], [prevents disease], [helps the baby survive the dangers of early life])

#mcq(7, [A vaccine usually contains], [weakened, killed or fragmentary antigens of the pathogen], [ready-made antibodies], [living virulent pathogens], [antibiotics])

#mcq(8, [The main reason food spoils faster in a hot climate is that], [the food contains more water], [the higher temperature speeds up microbial growth and enzyme action], [the food is exposed to more light], [the food contains more salt])

#mcq(9, [Which of these is a hallucinogen?], [Caffeine], [LSD], [Paracetamol], [Alcohol])

#mcq(10, [The best way to show the relationship between two measurements is a], [bar chart], [pie chart], [scatter graph with a line of best fit], [table only])

#mcq(11, [The three main parts of the brain are the], [cerebrum, spinal cord and nerves], [cerebellum, hypothalamus and pituitary], [medulla, heart and lungs], [cerebrum, cerebellum and medulla])

#mcq(12, [The ciliary muscles], [change the shape of the lens], [move the eyeball], [open and close the eyelid], [produce tears])

#mcq(13, [The hormone that stimulates the development of the mammary glands is], [insulin], [thyroxine], [prolactin], [adrenaline])

#mcq(14, [Wind-pollinated flowers are characterised by], [bright petals and scent], [large sticky pollen and nectar], [traps for insects], [small dull flowers with abundant light pollen])

#mcq(15, [Blood in the umbilical artery carries], [deoxygenated blood and waste from the foetus to the placenta], [oxygen and food to the foetus], [hormones only], [no blood cells])

#mcq(16, [Which measurement would best show that a seedling has grown rather than merely absorbed water?], [Height of the shoot], [Dry mass], [Number of leaves], [Colour of the leaves])

#mcq(17, [A disease that can be passed from one person to another is described as], [deficiency], [infectious], [hereditary], [degenerative])

#mcq(18, [Food is preserved by drying because], [the food becomes lighter], [the food becomes acidic], [removal of water stops microbial growth], [the food becomes colder])

#mcq(19, [A splint is used in first aid to], [immobilise a fractured limb], [stop bleeding], [clean a wound], [reduce a fever])

#mcq(20, [The part of the microscope that holds the objective lenses and allows them to be changed is the], [stage], [condenser], [base], [revolving nosepiece])

#mcq(21, [Which part of a neurone contains the nucleus and most of the cytoplasm?], [The axon], [The cell body], [The myelin sheath], [The terminal knob])

#mcq(22, [Tears contain lysozyme, which], [kills bacteria on the surface of the eye], [dissolves the cornea], [lubricates the lens], [produces colour vision])

#mcq(23, [The endocrine system and the nervous system are similar in that both], [use the blood to carry messages], [act within milliseconds], [are under voluntary control], [coordinate and control body activities])

#mcq(24, [The radicle of the embryo develops into the], [shoot], [leaf], [root], [flower])

#mcq(25, [Sperm are produced in the], [prostate gland], [testes], [epididymis], [vas deferens])

#mcq(26, [In humans, growth in height stops when], [the pituitary stops working], [the bones stop making blood], [the growth plates fuse], [the muscles stop growing])

#mcq(27, [The first line of defence against pathogens includes], [antibodies in the blood], [memory cells], [the spleen], [the intact skin and mucous membranes])

#mcq(28, [Fungi reproduce mainly by], [spores], [binary fission], [seeds], [eggs])

#mcq(29, [Paracetamol is classed as], [an analgesic], [a stimulant], [a hallucinogen], [a depressant])

#mcq(30, [A ×5 eyepiece with a ×10 objective gives a total magnification of], [×2], [×15], [×500], [×50])

#mcq(31, [The cerebrum is responsible for], [balance only], [intelligence, memory, reasoning and voluntary movement], [breathing only], [reflexes only])

#mcq(32, [A person who cannot hear high-pitched sounds may have damage to the], [outer ear], [eardrum only], [cochlea], [Eustachian tube])

#mcq(33, [Diabetes mellitus is caused by], [too much insulin], [too much glucagon only], [a deficiency of insulin or a failure of cells to respond to it], [a lack of iodine])

#mcq(34, [After fertilisation the ovary becomes the], [seed], [fruit], [embryo sac], [cotyledon])

#mcq(35, [The natural (rhythm) method of birth control relies on], [abstinence during the days around ovulation], [barrier devices], [hormone injections], [surgery])

#mcq(36, [In an insect, the stage between two moults is called an], [imago], [pupa], [larva], [instar])

#mcq(37, [The secondary immune response is], [faster and larger than the primary], [slower and smaller than the primary], [identical to the primary], [absent in vaccinated people])

#mcq(38, [The three groups of micro-organism studied in this chapter are], [bacteria, algae and protozoa], [viruses, worms and insects], [bacteria, viruses and fungi], [fungi, mosses and ferns])

#mcq(39, [Which of these is a notifiable disease in most countries?], [The common cold], [Cholera], [A mild headache], [A sprained ankle])

#mcq(40, [The fine adjustment knob is used], [before the coarse knob], [to change the objective], [to switch on the light], [to sharpen the image after the coarse focus])

